<%# Public profile screen — faithful port of the legacy SPA `UserProfile.jsx`:
    the gradient header card (owner edit surfaced via the settings gear — Hoojah
    2026 redesign Phase 4, Task 4.4), then the conviction card + live-debate card
    (owner only, both gated the same way as the tabbed list below), then the
    Hoojahs / Responses / Debates count tabs (Phase 4.5) with a framed list beneath.

    The tab bar and `<turbo-frame id="profile-list">` below are an ENHANCEMENT, not
    a requirement: each tab is a plain `link_to ... ?tab=<key>`, so a JS-off visit
    still navigates (full page reload) and lands on the right tab server-side —
    `data: {turbo_frame: "profile-list"}` only makes Turbo, when present, replace
    just the frame instead of the whole page.

    The frame carries `target: "_top"` so that links to OTHER pages inside it (a
    hoojah card, a debate card, an author byline, the empty-state CTA) perform a
    full-page visit rather than asking Turbo for a matching `profile-list` frame on
    the destination — which has none, so Turbo would render "Content missing"
    instead of navigating. The tab links keep their explicit
    `data: {turbo_frame: "profile-list"}`, which overrides the frame default and so
    still swaps only the frame. Same fix as the trending frame
    (spec/system/trending_navigation_spec.rb); guarded by
    spec/system/profile_navigation_spec.rb. %>
<%= render "shared/navbar" %>

<main class="max-w-xl mx-auto px-4 py-6">
  <div class="relative flex justify-center shadow">
    <%# Slice 7b (Gate 4): a private account the viewer can't see renders the gated
        header (no hoojah list). The owner always sees their own full profile + editor —
        `visible_to?` is true for self, so `@gated` is never true for the owner, and the
        owner's edit dialog trigger lives INSIDE `profile_header` now (the settings gear
        in its action bar), not as a sibling render here. %>
    <% if @gated %>
      <%= render "gated_header", user: @user %>
    <% else %>
      <%= render "profile_header", user: @user %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <% unless @gated %>
    <div class="mt-2 flex flex-col gap-2">
      <%= render "conviction_card", user: @user %>
      <%# LEAK PREVENTION: `@active_debate` is nil both when the owner has no active
          debate AND when the leak filter in `UsersController#owner_visible_active_debate`
          excluded it (a private/blocked co-debater), so this render is safe unconditionally. %>
      <% if @active_debate %>
        <%= render "live_debate_card", debate: @active_debate, user: @user %>
      <% end %>

      <%= render "profile_tabs", user: @user, active_tab: @active_tab,
            hoojahs_count: @hoojahs_count, responses_count: @responses_count, debates_count: @debates_count %>

      <%= turbo_frame_tag "profile-list", target: "_top", class: "flex flex-col gap-2 mt-2" do %>
        <% if @list.any? %>
          <% if @active_tab == "debates" %>
            <%= render partial: "debates/debate_card", collection: @list, as: :debate %>
          <% else %>
            <%# Both the Hoojahs and Responses tabs are `Hujah` records — a reply
                renders through the same compact card as a top-level claim, which
                already reads fine for either shape (avatar/handle/body/counts). %>
            <%= render partial: "user_hujah", collection: @list, as: :hujah %>
          <% end %>
        <% else %>
          <%# `ui/_empty_state`'s baked-in `p-3 bg-white` and faint tone are exactly what
              this row spelled by hand; the only thing lost is a dead `card-body` class
              left over from the Bootstrap SPA, which matches no rule in the bundle.

              Debates gets `swords` (matching the same "No debates yet" empty state on
              the hujah page) instead of the default `message-circle` glyph. The owner,
              on an empty Hoojahs tab only, gets a first-run CTA into the composer —
              a visitor or the Responses/Debates tabs fall back to the bare sentence. %>
          <% empty = {"hoojahs" => {message: "No hoojahs yet", icon: "message-circle"},
               "responses" => {message: "No responses yet", icon: "message-circle"},
               "debates" => {message: "No debates yet", icon: "swords"}}.fetch(@active_tab) %>
          <% if @active_tab == "hoojahs" && @user == current_user %>
            <%= render "ui/empty_state", message: empty[:message], icon: empty[:icon],
                  align: :center, cta_label: "Post your first hoojah", cta_href: new_hujah_path %>
          <% else %>
            <%= render "ui/empty_state", message: empty[:message], icon: empty[:icon] %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</main>
